      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As you stated it *should* be very unlikely to ever hit that limit but there should be a documented number regardless. \n\nHowever, it unfortunately can be common with projects that have made a lot of network changes between builds. It appears the Network ID Utility just assigns a new incremented ID without checking if there are spaces available from previously deleted objects. Though it's more likely the Network ID still exists but with a missing object reference. Manually solving or regenerating the IDs fixes those issues but performance and possible VRC Player Object persistence data loss makes the tool unreliable.\n\nI recommend using my tool as an alternative for those struggling with the current official tool. It will show you where problems are occurring, or you can simply just auto fix the issues and be on your way with building:\n\nhttps://github.com/BobyStar/OpenNID",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
